# 3. Scale up

## Description
This document outlines the architecture and specifics of a scaled-up, highly available web infrastructure hosting www.foobar.com with clustered load balancers and separated server tiers.

## Infrastructure Components
* **2 Load-balancers (HAProxy)** configured in a high-availability cluster.
* **Dedicated Servers** separating components:
  * Dedicated Web Server nodes (Nginx)
  * Dedicated Application Server nodes
  * Dedicated Database nodes (MySQL Primary-Replica cluster)

## Additional Elements & Reasons
* **Second Load-Balancer:** Added to ensure high availability and eliminate the load balancer as a Single Point of Failure (SPOF).
* **Split Components (Dedicated Servers):** Web servers, application servers, and databases are separated onto independent servers to eliminate resource competition, optimize performance, and allow independent scaling.

## Specifics & Explanations
* **Workload Isolation:** Separating tiers ensures that heavy database queries or application computations do not starve the web server of resources (CPU, RAM, and I/O).
